# Wireframe: App Shell (Sidebar Collapsed)

## Purpose & Flow Context

Alternate sidebar state on desktop/tablet viewports (>768px) where the sidebar reduces to icon-only width. Entry: user clicks the collapse toggle in the sidebar footer while on any page. Exit: user clicks the expand toggle to restore full sidebar, or resizes to mobile (<768px). Persists across navigation and page refresh.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

Same as App Shell (Desktop). Only sidebar-specific differences noted.

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Same 12-column layout as desktop shell. Spacing cadence: 4px dense for collapsed sidebar.

**App-shell**: Shared header + collapsed sidebar + expanded content area.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Same as desktop: search, notification bell, user avatar, theme toggle | Unchanged from expanded layout |
| Sidebar (collapsed) | Team selector icon, nav link icons only, expand toggle | Width: 56px; labels hidden |
| Content | Main page content — fills reclaimed sidebar width | Wider than expanded layout |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Header — global triggers
2. Content — primary task (now more horizontal space)
3. Sidebar — navigation cues (icons only)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [search] [theme-toggle] [bell 3] [avatar]              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- S --+  +-- Content (fills remaining, wider) --------------+  |
|  |  [T]  |  |  [h1 Page Title]                                |  |
|  |       |  |                                                    |  |
|  |  [I]  |  |  (Page-specific content — now uses               |  |
|  |  [P]  |  |   reclaimed horizontal space)                    |  |
|  |  [C]  |  |                                                    |  |
|  |       |  |                                                    |  |
|  |  [>>] |  |                                                    |  |
|  +-------+  +----------------------------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: S=Team selector icon, I=Issues icon, P=Projects icon, C=Cycles icon, >>=Expand button*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Collapsed sidebar container | Sidebar (collapsed variant) | Width 56px; shows icons only; aria-label="Main navigation" | — |
| Team selector (collapsed) | TeamSelector (collapsed) | Icon only; tooltip shows team name on hover/focus | aria-label="Current team: {name}" |
| Nav link (collapsed) | NavLink (collapsed) | Icon only; tooltip shows label on hover/focus | aria-label matches link label; aria-current="page" on active |
| Expand toggle | SidebarToggle | aria-label="Expand sidebar"; icon chevron points right | — |
| Content area | (main) | Fills available width; overflow-y: auto | Adjusted width on transition |

## Data Display

No data display — icons only. The collapsed sidebar is a navigation affordance, not a data container.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Nav link tooltip | Full link label (e.g. "Issues") | Visible on hover/focus — labelled via title or aria-describedby |
| Expand toggle | "Expand sidebar" | Action-oriented label |
| Team selector tooltip | "Team Name" | Team name context on hover |

## States

### Populated (Default)

Layout as shown in ASCII sketch. Content area is wider than expanded state.

### Empty

N/A — collapsed sidebar always shows icons.

### Loading

Same skeleton as desktop shell, just with narrower sidebar region.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [search] [theme-toggle] [bell] [avatar]                |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-S+  +-- Content (fills remaining, wider) -------------------+  |
|  |[T]|  |  [===== skeleton bar =====]                          |  |
|  |[I]|  |  [=== skeleton ===]                                  |  |
|  |[P]|  |  [======== skeleton =========]                       |  |
|  |[C]|  |  [=== skeleton ===]                                  |  |
|  |[>>]|  |                                                      |  |
|  +---+  +------------------------------------------------------+  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

Layout shell does not have an error state. Page errors appear in content area.

### Success / Confirmation

Visual feedback: sidebar width animates on collapse/expand transition. Instant response to toggle click.

### Transition (Collapse ↔ Expand)

```
[Before]                               [After]
+-- Sidebar (240px) --+                +-- S(56px) --+
|  Team Name      ▼   |                |  [T]        |
|  Issues    ●        |   → click →    |  [I]        |
|  Projects           |                |  [P]        |
|  Cycles             |                |  [C]        |
|                     |                |             |
|  [<< Collapse]      |                |  [>> Expand] |
+---------------------+                +-------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Collapsed sidebar as described; can be expanded |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same behavior; collapsed sidebar persists across page navigation |
| Mobile (<768px) | Collapsed state irrelevant — sidebar is hidden; hamburger replaces toggle |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | Same as desktop: header role="banner", nav role="navigation", main role="main" |
| Heading order | Same as desktop — layout has no heading; page content provides h1 |
| Reading / Focus order | Header → Sidebar (collapsed) → Content — tabbing through sidebar visits each icon in order |
| Accessible names | Every icon-only element gets aria-label describing its action/destination |
| Keyboard operability | Tab moves through sidebar icons; tooltips appear on focus; Enter/Space activates link/toggle |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation; sidebar icons have adequate hit area within 56px width |
| Focus not obscured | No overlapping issue; sidebar and header do not obscure focused elements |
| Non-color intent | Active link uses different icon fill/background; expand toggle uses icon direction change |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*
